# pyproject.toml here holds ruff settings and nothing else: no [project] table,
# because this is an application rather than a distributable package. Vercel's
# Python builder sees the file and hands it to `uv lock`, which fails on the
# missing table. Keeping it out of the bundle lets the builder fall back to
# requirements.txt, which is where the pinned dependencies actually live.
pyproject.toml
